# Resource workflow — synthetic test fixture

[I-001]: How should the resource workflow work within the existing access model? #issue { "status": "open", "parent": null }

## Navigation

[I-010]: What defines primary navigation? #issue { "status": "resolved", "parent": "I-001", "resolved_by": "D-006", "resolution_history": ["D-006"] }

[P-010A]: Workspaces define the root navigation hierarchy. #position { "status": "rejected", "issue": "I-010", "rejection_reason": "Cross-workspace work and a large workspace count make the hierarchy inefficient." }

[P-010B]: Operational areas define navigation; workspace is a context switcher. #position { "status": "accepted", "issue": "I-010" }
    + [E-021]
    + [C-008]
    + [C-012]
    + <A-004>

[E-021]: Users perform workflows that span workspaces. #evidence { "status": "verified", "issue": "I-010", "sources": [{ "kind": "user", "ref": "Fixture scenario: daily cross-workspace user work", "authority": "intent" }], "handoff": "existing" }

[C-008]: The navigation must remain usable with thirty workspaces. #constraint { "status": "agreed", "sources": [{ "kind": "user", "ref": "Fixture scale envelope: thirty workspaces", "authority": "intent" }], "handoff": "invariant" }

[C-012]: Navigation must never imply access to workspaces the user is not assigned to. #constraint { "status": "verified", "issue": "I-010", "sources": [{ "kind": "spec", "ref": "specs/access.md", "authority": "normative", "locator": "Fixture staff-access contract" }], "handoff": "invariant" }

<A-004>: A workspace hierarchy adds repeated navigation for cross-workspace work; a context switcher retains workspace awareness. #argument { "status": "active", "issue": "I-010", "based_on": ["E-021", "C-008"] }

[D-006]: Use operations-first navigation and retain persistent, explicit workspace context alongside operational navigation. #decision { "status": "accepted", "resolves": ["I-010"], "basis": "user", "selected": ["P-010B"], "alternatives": ["P-010A"], "based_on": ["E-021", "C-008", "C-012", "A-004"], "rationale": "This supports cross-workspace workflows and the stated scale while retaining workspace awareness. Role-derived access remains authoritative.", "sources": [{ "kind": "user", "ref": "Fixture agreement: operations-first navigation with a persistent workspace context switcher", "authority": "intent" }] }

[Q-001]: Cross-workspace workflows need an explicit way to show their scope. #consequence { "status": "current", "derives_from": "D-006", "handoff": "target" }

## Open design detail

[I-014]: What visual treatment identifies the current workspace context? #issue { "status": "deferred", "parent": "I-010", "blocking": false, "nonblocking_reason": "The behavior and authorization semantics are settled; visual styling can be chosen during interaction design without selecting a different scope model." }
